# No guess is opened, so each call is a call of what was read. Function.prototype.call and apply refuse a receiver that is no function, and apply a list that is none: in there the frame on top is theirs,
# and the error could not say how the program writes the call. So what was read under `call` or `apply` is looked at in front of the call, wherever the call stands:
# a closure as it was created is neither of the two; anything else goes to the stub, on a rare way. The read is not left to the stub that reads and calls.
# RUN(KEPT): emit f1 mechanisms=none
# KEPT: Void {{*}} = Patch(
# KEPT: = Load8S({{*}}AOTSlimClosure_word
# RUN(LAST): emit f2 mechanisms=none
# LAST: Void {{*}} = Patch(
# LAST: = Load8S({{*}}AOTSlimClosure_word
# RUN(CALLED): emit f3 mechanisms=none
# CALLED: Void {{*}} = Patch(
# CALLED: = Load8S({{*}}AOTSlimClosure_word
# Under any other name one stub reads and calls, as ever.
# RUN(OTHER): emit f4 mechanisms=none
# OTHER-NOT: = Load8S(
